# [K66] REGRESSION — ON A VM ROUTE WITH NO DFA SCAN IN FRONT, A NECESSARY RUN
# LONGER THAN THE PRE-CHECK'S 8-BYTE WINDOW IS COMPARED WHOLE, SO WHETHER A
# HOSTILE SUBJECT ANSWERS NOMATCH OR GIVES UP NO LONGER DEPENDS ON WHICH
# WINDOW THE PRIOR CHOSE (docs/dev/known_issues.md K66; docs/spec/tuning.md
# §2.29; K65's fix (a) extended to runs, Frank's ruling 2026-09-25).
#
# The backreference declines the hybrid, so the artifact is a FRAMED VM
# program (`RX_VM_PREFILTER "none"`) and the pre-check is its only linear
# no-match proof. The necessary run is the 16 bytes `eeeeeeee~#~#~#~#`; the
# pre-check's window (`RX_REQ_RUN`) is `~#~#~#~#` under `encoding byte` (the
# frequency prior) and `eeeeeeee` under `encoding utf8` (the leftmost
# fallback). On a class run of 16..18 letters, `([a-z]+)+` backtracks
# exponentially before the absent run fails the attempt, so with only the
# window compared (and K65's whole-set half, which every subject here
# satisfies: each holds `e`, `~` and `#`) a block GAVE UP (`steps`) on every
# subject holding its own window and not the whole run: under byte the
# `e...~#~#~#~#` cells, under utf8 the `...eeeeeeee~#` cells, and under both
# the `...eeeeeeee!~#~#~#~#` cells, which hold BOTH windows and still not the
# run. Every `n` cell is NOMATCH in PCRE2 and must be NOMATCH here under
# either encoding. The byte block's scan member sits at offset 8 of the
# whole run and the utf8 block's at offset 0, so both window-guard shapes of
# the whole-run compare are exercised.
#
# The `gu` cells are the CONTROL that the budget really reaches the VM: with
# the whole run present no pre-check can help and the same class run still
# exhausts the block's budget. They prove the `n` cells pass because of the
# pre-check, not because 10000 steps happened to be enough. `budget
# steps=10000` and class runs of 16..18 letters keep the failing direction to
# milliseconds and let python `re` verify every cell; the 16-byte `!` tail
# keeps the VM's minimum-remaining-length prune from cutting the backtracking
# short, which at these lengths would otherwise hide the defect. (tests/codegen/run_prechecks.sh §5.8
# asserts the emitted whole-run text; this file asserts the answers.)

pattern (x?)([a-z]+)+eeeeeeee~#~#~#~#\1
features backrefs
encoding byte
budget steps=10000
n "eaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa~#~#~#~#!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!"
n "eaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa~#~#~#~#!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!"
n "aaaaaaaaeeeeeeee~#!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!"
n "aaaaaaaaaaeeeeeeee~#!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!"
n "aaaaaaaaeeeeeeee!~#~#~#~#!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!"
n "aaaaaaaaaaeeeeeeee!~#~#~#~#!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!"
m "abceeeeeeee~#~#~#~#" 0 19
gu steps "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaZb!eeeeeeee~#~#~#~#"

pattern (x?)([a-z]+)+eeeeeeee~#~#~#~#\1
features backrefs
encoding utf8
budget steps=10000
n "eaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa~#~#~#~#!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!"
n "eaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa~#~#~#~#!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!"
n "aaaaaaaaeeeeeeee~#!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!"
n "aaaaaaaaaaeeeeeeee~#!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!"
n "aaaaaaaaeeeeeeee!~#~#~#~#!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!"
n "aaaaaaaaaaeeeeeeee!~#~#~#~#!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!"
m "abceeeeeeee~#~#~#~#" 0 19
gu steps "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaZb!eeeeeeee~#~#~#~#"
